    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41386" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rē-splendĕo</span></b> ,
			ēre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to shine brightly; to glitter</i>,
				<i>be resplendent</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fulvā resplendent fragmina
					harenā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 12, 741</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sil. 12, 732</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Q. N. 1, 13, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros.
				3, 446</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Agam. 543</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sidera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Manil. 5, 719</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Matt. 17, 2</span></i>
			.— <b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">resplendet gloria Martis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Laud. Stil. 1, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
